{"id":"tiffany-coates","title":"Tiffany Coates and Thelma: Cape Town to Cairo","who":"Tiffany Coates (with Becky Lincoln, then Maggie)","when":"About 2000 (part of a ride that began in 1997)","vehicle":"BMW R80GS \"Thelma\" (1992)","kind":"moto","color":"#ca8a04","summary":"Two friends with no riding experience and £2,500 between them bought a second-hand BMW R80GS in 1997 to ride to India; nine months turned into years. After Australia, Becky went home to university and Tiffany shipped Thelma to Cape Town, where her friend Maggie flew in to ride up Africa with her: the classic Cape to Cairo, with detours. That section is mapped here. Later she rode the length of the Americas and across northern Asia to Mongolia, more than 200,000 miles on the same bike; today she leads motorcycle tours and is a Churchill Fellow.","sources":[{"label":"Overland Expo: Community Spotlight, Tiffany Coates","url":"https://www.overlandexpo.com/compass/communitycoates"},{"label":"Exploring Overland: Tiffany Coates' R80GS, Thelma","url":"https://exploringoverland.com/overland-tech-travel/2012/3/2/no-poseur-machine-tiffany-coates-r80gs-thelma.html"},{"label":"Team Motorcycle: interview","url":"https://www.teammotorcycle.com/blog/tiffany-coates-motorcycle-interview"},{"label":"Churchill Fellowship: Tiffany Coates","url":"https://www.churchillfellowship.org/ideas-experts/fellows-directory/tiffany-coates/"}],"approximate":"Only the start, the region and the end named in interviews; the road between them is the usual Cape to Cairo route, not hers.","km":9770,"bbox":[18.4171,-33.9287,39.1505,30.0441],"stops":[{"name":"Cape Town","place":"Cape Town, South Africa","at":[-33.9288,18.4172],"date":"c. 2000","text":"Thelma shipped to Africa; Maggie flies in from Ireland to join.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Camps_bay_%2853460319478%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Camps_bay_%2853460319478%29_%28cropped%29.jpg","page":"Cape Town","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Camps_bay_%2853460319478%29_%28cropped%29.jpg","credit":"Der Berzerker from Washington, DC, USA","license":"CC BY-SA 2.0"}},{"name":"East Africa","place":"Nairobi, Kenya","at":[-1.289,36.8173],"text":"North up the classic Cape to Cairo route, with diversions.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Nairobi_skyline_from_Gem_Hotel.jpg/500px-Nairobi_skyline_from_Gem_Hotel.jpg","page":"Nairobi","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nairobi_skyline_from_Gem_Hotel.jpg","credit":"Daniel Case","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Cairo","place":"Cairo, Egypt","at":[30.0444,31.2357],"text":"The top of Africa.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Cairo%E2%80%99s_Qasr_El_Nil_Bridge.jpg/500px-Cairo%E2%80%99s_Qasr_El_Nil_Bridge.jpg","page":"Cairo","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cairo%E2%80%99s_Qasr_El_Nil_Bridge.jpg","credit":"سها القاضي","license":"CC0"}}],"legs":[{"by":"ride","km":5226,"line":[[-33.9287,18.4171],[-33.9154,18.491],[-33.8854,18.529],[-33.8865,18.6355],[-33.8376,18.7278],[-33.7832,18.9459],[-33.7418,19.0064],[-33.7234,19.1797],[-33.6993,19.2083],[-33.7046,19.2559],[-33.6554,19.2891],[-33.6339,19.3243],[-33.6153,19.5077],[-33.5611,19.5109],[-33.5288,19.5437],[-33.5047,19.5818],[-33.4787,19.6859],[-33.4137,19.7327],[-33.3954,19.7939],[-33.401,19.9235],[-33.3161,20.0457],[-33.2616,20.1699],[-33.2632,20.2682],[-33.2279,20.5652],[-33.1818,20.7125],[-33.1966,20.8592],[-33.1246,21.2144],[-33.0928,21.5737],[-32.932,21.7344],[-32.8583,21.945],[-32.7734,21.9753],[-32.7402,22.0045],[-32.5096,22.2995],[-32.362,22.5449],[-32.3596,22.5823],[-32.3328,22.5838],[-32.2066,22.848],[-32.0449,22.9729],[-32.0238,23.0071],[-31.9372,23.0362],[-31.8909,23.069],[-31.8857,23.2252],[-31.8093,23.365],[-31.7264,23.4373],[-31.6663,23.4637],[-31.5104,23.6168],[-31.4453,23.8807],[-31.3321,24.0997],[-31.2191,24.2644],[-31.0729,24.4352],[-30.9847,24.6019],[-30.9009,24.8117],[-30.7